module

public import Sheaf.RingTheory.PopescuLiftPresentation
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.LocalRing.ResidueField.Fiber

/-! # Smooth fibres of the prepared Popescu quotient on a chart

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 07CP, computation modulo pi on a chart and the coefficient
calculation comparing the different charts.
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-popescu-lift-chart-fibres).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe a c

namespace Algebra

/-- The special fibre and the residue-field fibre are smooth on each prepared chart.
No annihilator hypothesis is needed for this calculation modulo pi.

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 07CP (lemma-lifting), the displayed polynomial description
of `(D_k/pi D_k)_{a_k}` and the subsequent coefficient calculation for other charts.
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-popescu-lift-chart-fibres).

Proof: Write P=R[x], Q=P[z], u_l=f_l-pi z_l, and
p_{kl}=a_k z_l-sum_{j in E_k} h_{klj} z_j-pi g_{kl}. Work modulo pi and invert a_k.
The cleared relations imply that all f_l are generated by the f_j with j in E_k.
The equations p_{kl}=0 eliminate the z_l outside E_k. For another chart k', the
coefficient of z_j in the remaining relation, after multiplying by a_k, is
b_j=a_{k'}h_{klj}-sum_{j' in E_{k'}}h_{k'lj'}h_{kj'j}. The two expressions for
 a_{k'}a_k f_l give sum b_j f_j=0 in the reduced conormal module localized at a_k.
Its specified basis implies that each b_j is zero in Cbar localized at a_k.
Thus it remains zero modulo pi. The relations from all other charts impose no further
conditions, and (D/pi D)_{a_k} is the polynomial algebra in z_j, j in E_k, over
(Cbar/pi Cbar)_{a_k}. The presentation surjectivity, the values on X_i, and the
compatibility of cmod identify the coefficient map with the map specified here.
Polynomial algebras and principal localizations are smooth, proving the second clause.
The coefficient algebra is smooth over R/pi by base change from the smooth reduced
chart in Prepared.smooth. Its polynomial extension is therefore smooth over R/pi.
Let p be the contraction to R of qD. Since pi is zero in the residue field of p,
base change of this smooth chart to that field is the fibre algebra of R to D
localized at the image of a_k. The fibre prime contracts to qD, so the image of a_k
avoids it. That principal localization witnesses the first clause. ULift transports
these identifications without changing the equations or generator values. -/
theorem popescu_lift_chart_fibres (R : Type a) (Cbar : Type c)
    [CommRing R] [CommRing Cbar] [Algebra R Cbar] (π : R)
    [Algebra (R ⧸ Ideal.span ({π ^ 2} : Set R)) Cbar]
    [IsScalarTower R (R ⧸ Ideal.span ({π ^ 2} : Set R)) Cbar]
    (d : PopescuLiftPresentation R Cbar π) (hd : d.Prepared)
    (c : Cbar →ₐ[R] (d.liftingAlgebra ⧸
      Ideal.span ({algebraMap R d.liftingAlgebra π} : Set d.liftingAlgebra)))
    (cmod : (Cbar ⧸ Ideal.span ({algebraMap R Cbar π} : Set Cbar)) →+*
      (d.liftingAlgebra ⧸
        Ideal.span ({algebraMap R d.liftingAlgebra π} : Set d.liftingAlgebra)))
    (hc : ∀ i : Fin d.n, c (d.ε (MvPolynomial.X i)) = Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (d.x i))
    (hcmod : cmod.comp (Ideal.Quotient.mk _) = c.toRingHom)
    (q : PrimeSpectrum (d.liftingAlgebra ⧸
      Ideal.span ({algebraMap R d.liftingAlgebra π} : Set d.liftingAlgebra)))
    (k : Fin d.r) (hk : c (d.ε (d.reduced (d.a k))) ∉ q.asIdeal) :
    let qD := PrimeSpectrum.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk _) q
    let p := PrimeSpectrum.comap (algebraMap R d.liftingAlgebra) qD
    IsSmoothAtPrime p.asIdeal.ResidueField
      (PrimeSpectrum.preimageEquivFiber R d.liftingAlgebra p ⟨qD, rfl⟩) ∧
    @Smooth (Cbar ⧸ Ideal.span ({algebraMap R Cbar π} : Set Cbar)) _
      (Localization.Away (c (d.ε (d.reduced (d.a k))))) _
      (letI := cmod.toAlgebra; inferInstance) := by sorry

end Algebra
